@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+This document records how the site minimises data collection, which third parties it
+uses (none at the moment), and which browser policies enforce that. Update it whenever
+a form, script, embed, or header changes.
+
+## 1. Data inventory (data minimisation & purpose limitation)
+
+| Data | Where collected | Purpose (only use) | Retention | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Email address | Newsletter form (`/newsletter`) | Sending the weekly newsletter | Deleted on unsubscribe | Only field collected. No name or birthday. Purpose stated next to the field. No pre-ticked boxes. |
+| Session cookie | Login (backend) | Keeping the user signed in | Session; cleared on logout | Must be `__Host-session; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/` (see §4). |
+| Security reports | `/api/security-reports` | Detecting CSP/connection policy violations | ≤ 30 days | Strip query strings, emails and tokens before storing. |
+
+Not collected: precise location (the store finder should take a city or postcode, not
+the Geolocation API, which is disabled in `Permissions-Policy`), device fingerprints,
+full user-agent strings, or third-party advertising identifiers.
+
+`assets/js/app.js` removes marketing parameters (`utm_*`, `gclid`, `fbclid`, `msclkid`, …)
+from the address bar so they aren't bookmarked or shared onward.
+
+## 2. Third-party audit
+
+| Resource | Status | Action taken |
+|---|---|---|
+| Hero image from `images.unsplash.com` (hotlinked) | **Removed** | Sent every visitor's IP, UA and referrer to Unsplash's CDN. Replaced with self-hosted copies in `assets/img/` (Unsplash photo `1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085`, Unsplash License). |
+| Analytics / tag managers | None | Don't add any without a privacy review. If you need metrics, prefer aggregate first-party, cookieless measurement. |
+| Social widgets / share SDKs | None | If you need sharing, use plain `<a href>` intent links with `rel="noopener noreferrer"`. |
+| Video/map embeds | None | If you add one, use a click-to-load façade and privacy-enhanced domains (e.g. `youtube-nocookie.com`), and update `frame-src` and `Permissions-Policy`. |
+| Web fonts | None (system font stack) | Self-host any future fonts. Don't use third-party font CDNs. |
+
+The CSP (`default-src 'none'` with only `'self'` exceptions) and `Connection-Allowlist:
+(response-origin)` block any new third-party request until someone deliberately updates
+this file and the headers.
+
+**How to repeat the audit:** open DevTools → Network, reload with cache disabled, and
+filter by "third-party" (or export a HAR). Every request should be same-origin. Also check
+the Issues panel and `/api/security-reports` for violations.
+
+## 3. Response headers (`_headers`, mirrored in `<meta>` where possible)
+
+- **Content-Security-Policy**: first-party scripts, styles, images, fonts and fetches only. Also sets `form-action 'self'`, `base-uri 'none'`, `object-src 'none'` and `frame-ancestors 'none'`. Trusted Types is enforced with no policies (`trusted-types 'none'`), so the app can't use `innerHTML`-style sinks at all. Violations go to `report-to`.
+- **Connection-Allowlist**: blocks *all* outbound connections except our own origin, including `dns-prefetch`, `preconnect` and WebRTC, which CSP doesn't cover. Only Chromium supports it; CSP is the cross-browser baseline.
+- **Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin**: paths and query strings never leak to other sites.
+- **Permissions-Policy**: turns off sensors, camera, microphone, geolocation, Topics/FLEDGE/attribution APIs, autoplay and more. Only `payment` and passkey sign-in (`publickey-credentials-get`) are kept, for our own origin.
+- **HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, COOP (`same-origin-allow-popups`), CORP (`same-origin`)**: transport security and cross-origin isolation.
+- **Clear-Site-Data** on `/logout`: wipes cookies and storage. Logout is now a POST form, so other sites can't trigger it.
+- **Cache-Control: no-store** on account, rewards, ordering and form endpoints.
+- **`/.well-known/gpc.json`**: declares that we honour Global Privacy Control. The page also tells users when their browser sends the GPC signal.
+
+## 4. Backend requirements (not enforceable from static files)
+
+- Session cookie: `Set-Cookie: __Host-session=…; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`.
+- `/logout` must accept **POST only**, invalidate the session server-side, and return `Clear-Site-Data`.
+- `/newsletter` must use double opt-in and rate limiting, keep the address only for that purpose, and hard-delete it on unsubscribe.
+- Remove personal data (emails, tokens, IPs) from application logs and security reports.
+- `/account/privacy` must let signed-in users download, correct and delete their data, with no support ticket needed.
+- Never put tokens or personal data in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`. The client script clears both on logout as a backstop.
